From: Andrei Gosman <andrei.gosman@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-09-03
Subject: [PATCH 019/NNN] build: make the C++ standard selectable

The tree pins -std=c++14. UHD 4.7 and later use std::is_same_v and
std::is_arithmetic_v in its public headers, which are C++17, so a build
against a recent UHD fails inside uhd/utils/cast.hpp and
uhd/rfnoc/actions.hpp before reaching any code here.

Passing -std=c++17 on the command line does not help, because the pinned
flag is appended afterwards and the last one wins. Turning it into a cache
variable leaves the default at c++14 and lets a build that needs the newer
standard ask for it.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt	2026-09-03 15:50:59
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt	2026-09-03 15:50:59
@@ -372,7 +372,11 @@
 endmacro(ADD_C_COMPILER_FLAG_IF_AVAILABLE)
 
 if(CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "GNU" OR CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "Clang")
-  set(CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS "${CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS} -Wall -Wno-comment -Wno-reorder -Wno-unused-variable -Wtype-limits -std=c++14 -fno-strict-aliasing")
+  # UHD 4.7 and later use std::is_same_v and friends in its public headers,
+  # which are C++17. The tree itself still builds as C++14, so the standard is
+  # a knob rather than a hard change.
+  set(SRSRAN_CXX_STANDARD "c++14" CACHE STRING "C++ standard to build with")
+  set(CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS "${CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS} -Wall -Wno-comment -Wno-reorder -Wno-unused-variable -Wtype-limits -std=${SRSRAN_CXX_STANDARD} -fno-strict-aliasing")
 
   ADD_CXX_COMPILER_FLAG_IF_AVAILABLE("-Wno-unused-but-set-variable" HAVE_WNO_UNUSED_BUT_SET_VARIABLE)
 
